%I A401219 #11 Oct 19 2026 15:43:31
%S A401219 2,3,7,23,47,139,283,659,1319,10067,20147,120919,500947,1232213,
%T A401219 4076783,8153567,55443959,187814447,646611887
%N A401219 Smallest prime that has n distinct primes in its Pratt primality certificate.
%C A401219 a(n) is the least prime(k) such that A401218(k) = n.
%C A401219 Appears to be related to A366929. In particular, it seems that A366929(n+1)<=a(n) with equality when A366929(n+1) is prime.
%H A401219 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/PrattCertificate.html">Pratt Certificate</a>.
%o A401219 (PARI) \\ pset(p) defined in A401218
%o A401219 a(n) = forprime(p=2, oo, if(#pset(p)==n, return(p)))
%Y A401219 Cf. A037231, A366929, A401218.
%K A401219 nonn,more,new
%O A401219 1,1
%A A401219 _Andrew Howroyd_, Oct 19 2026
